  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2024 dataset documents the SIESTA-BdG implementation for solving Bogoliubov-de Gennes and density functional theory problems within SIESTA, supporting superconductivity research with a code-oriented, reproducible resource. The strongest evidence of uptake is methodological reuse: the record shows seven documented downstream reuse links, while citation and public-attention signals are still at zero.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset accompanies work on an integrated density functional Bogoliubov-de Gennes framework for superconductors, implemented in the SIESTA code. Its subject matter sits at the intersection of superconductivity, density functional theory, and computational physics, and the associated materials emphasize applications to inhomogeneous superconductors and heterostructures. The author group spans Utrecht University and the Institut Catal\u00e0 de Nanoci\u00e8ncia i Nanotecnologia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">What stands out in the record is reuse rather than citation. The dataset has seven documented downstream reuse links, all classified as associated articles, indicating that the resource is already embedded in a small but visible technical literature. The stewardship metadata also connects the dataset to related articles and software, including SIESTA and the AiiDA SIESTA plugin, which reinforces its role as supporting infrastructure for computational workflows.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the citation record is still early. OpenAlex currently shows zero citations, and the available scite and event-data signals are also at zero. That makes the downstream reuse evidence especially important: the dataset is being linked as a supplement to related scholarship even before a citation trail has formed.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The access and usage indicators are likewise quiet, with DataCite reporting zero views and zero downloads. Public discourse signals are unavailable in the archive, so the record does not yet show broader community discussion. Taken together, the dataset\u2019s impact is best described as early-stage scholarly reuse centered on computational superconductivity, with infrastructure value clearer than conventional citation impact at this point.</p>",
